<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  ALL OF THESE ARE GLOBAL, NOT adminhtml
  ===========================================================================
  BUSINESS.md section 12 makes the driver and vehicle details a hard
  precondition of `شحنتك في الطريق اليك`, on the grounds that the customer has
  no other route to them and the vehicle is already on the road.

  A rule that strong is declared in the GLOBAL area so it holds on every path
  that can write an order — the admin's comment form, /rest/V1/orders, a console
  script, a mass action. Scoping any of it to adminhtml would cover today's one
  screen and leave every future integration free to dispatch a shipment with no
  driver on it, or to invoice an order without moving it.

  ===========================================================================
  1. THE DISPATCH GATE
  ===========================================================================
  `sales_order_save_before` rather than a plugin on OrderRepositoryInterface:
  the admin's own status-change controller calls $order->save() directly and
  never touches the repository, so a repository plugin would have been bypassed
  by the exact screen the rule exists for. The observer class records the
  verified trace through core.

  ===========================================================================
  2. THE SNAPSHOT CHECK AT PLACEMENT
  ===========================================================================
  `sales_model_service_quote_submit_before` is the one moment where the quote
  and the order both exist and neither has been written yet — so it is the last
  point at which "this order says it is collected from a station" and "this
  order names no station" can be reconciled instead of being left to disagree
  for the life of the order.

  It repairs and never refuses; the observer's own header carries the reasoning,
  including why throwing here would make an admin-created depot order
  impossible to raise at all.

  ===========================================================================
  3. AXIS B FOLLOWS AXIS A: PAYMENT ACCEPTED MOVES THE ORDER
  ===========================================================================
  §2's transition table says station 0 -> station 1 happens on payment
  acceptance, automatically. Nothing implemented it: the customer's rail was
  right only because it falls back to `state === processing`, while the order
  itself never moved and the admin's status field still read "Processing" beside
  fully invoiced items — which §10 lists as a corrected defect and which was in
  fact only half corrected.

  `sales_order_invoice_register` fires inside Invoice::register() with the order
  in the payload and before it is saved, so the stamp rides the same write.

  ===========================================================================
  4. AXIS A FOLLOWS AXIS B: COLLECTION COMPLETES THE ORDER
  ===========================================================================
  Setting `تم الاستلام` moves the fulfilment stage and leaves the commercial
  state where it was, so an order stayed `processing` for ever — the grid said
  Processing, the "Ship" button stayed, and no report counted the sale as
  finished. Reaching the last station now raises the shipment that takes the
  order to `complete`.

  `sales_order_save_commit_after`, not `_save_after`: creating a shipment
  WRITES, and doing that inside the transaction of the save that triggered it
  is how a nested rollback loses both.
-->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:Event/etc/events.xsd">
    <event name="sales_order_save_before">
        <observer name="spartrak_pickup_require_consignment_before_dispatch"
                  instance="Spartrak\PickupLocation\Observer\RequireConsignmentBeforeDispatch"/>
    </event>
    <event name="sales_model_service_quote_submit_before">
        <observer name="spartrak_pickup_complete_snapshot_on_placement"
                  instance="Spartrak\PickupLocation\Observer\CompletePickupSnapshotOnPlacement"/>
    </event>
    <event name="sales_order_invoice_register">
        <observer name="spartrak_pickup_stamp_packed_on_payment_approval"
                  instance="Spartrak\PickupLocation\Observer\StampPackedOnPaymentApproval"/>
    </event>
    <event name="sales_order_save_commit_after">
        <observer name="spartrak_pickup_complete_order_on_collection"
                  instance="Spartrak\PickupLocation\Observer\CompleteOrderOnCollection"/>
    </event>
</config>
